<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bilbilis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Augusta Bilbilis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bilbilis was a Celtiberian and then Roman town on a hill near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calatayud">Calatayud</a> in Aragon, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It became a Roman municipium under Augustus, with a forum, temple and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a>, and was known for the iron worked from local ores. The poet Martial was born there around 40 CE and praised his home town in his epigrams.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bilbilis.jpg" alt="Bilbilis" width="320" height="241" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ciudad_romana_de_Bilbilis,_Calatayud,_Espa%C3%B1a_2012-05-16,_DD_05.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
